## 5. Phase D – Development (MVP Sprint Plan)
| Sprint | Duration | Key Tasks |
|--------|----------|-----------|
| **Sprint 1 – Foundations** | 1–2 weeks | Set up repo, CI/CD pipeline; choose tech stack; create DB schema; implement user registration & login. |
| **Sprint 2 – Product Catalogue** | 2 weeks | Build item CRUD for admin; public listing page with search/filter; image upload (responsive); basic styling. |
| **Sprint 3 – Shopping Cart & Checkout** | 2 weeks | Cart widget, checkout flow, integrate Paystack sandbox, order creation, email receipt, basic fraud checks. |
| **Sprint 4 – Order & Delivery Tracker** | 1–2 weeks | Order status lifecycle (pending → paid → shipped → delivered). “Mark as shipped” button for admin; simple tracking display. |
| **Sprint 5 – Polish & QA** | 1 week | Mobile responsiveness testing, image optimization, form validation, edge‑case bugs, basic security (XSS/CSRF, HTTPS). |
| **Sprint 6 – Soft Launch** | 1 week | Invite friends/family, collect feedback, iterate on UI/UX, add any missing filters (e.g., price range). |
| **Total Estimated Time** | **6‑8 weeks** (assuming ~20 hrs/week dev time). |

---
## 6. Phase E – Testing & QA
- **Functional Checklist**: registration, login, add‑to‑cart, payment (sandbox), order creation, status update, admin CRUD.
- **Usability Testing**: Recruit 5‑7 Ghanaian peers (mix of personas) to complete a purchase; record friction points, comment on size guide clarity, payment flow.
- **Performance**: Use Lighthouse to ensure <3 s page load on 3G throttling; optimize images, minify CSS/JS.
- **Security**: Parameterized queries (ORM), password hashing with bcrypt/Argon2, CSP headers, avoid storing raw card data (use Paystack/Flutterwave tokens).
- **Cross‑Browser**: Test on Chrome, Firefox, Safari (mobile), and Android WebView.

---
## 7. Phase F – Launch & Logistics Integration
### 7.1 Delivery Partners (Ghana)
| Partner | Service Type | Typical Transit (Accra) | Tracking |
|---------|--------------|------------------------|----------|
| **Ghana Post** | Economy parcel | 5‑7 days | Basic tracking number |
| **Flash Express** | Courier (city‑wide) | 2‑3 days | Real‑time tracking |
| **DHL eCommerce** | International/large parcels | 3‑5 days | Detailed tracking |
| **Ride‑hailing couriers** (Bolt, Uber) | Same‑day/next‑day (Accra/Kumasi) | Same day | Driver tracking + SMS |

### 7.2 Standard Operating Procedure (SOP)
1. **Order Received** → Verify payment status.
2. **Pack Dress** – include thank‑you note, care label if applicable.
3. **Attach Shipping Label** – partner label with order number.
4. **Handover to Partner** – obtain tracking number.
5. **Update System** – enter tracking number, change order status to “shipped”.
6. **Customer Notification** – SMS/USSD with tracking link (via Twilio or Bulksms Ghana).
7. **Delivery Confirmation** – partner marks delivered; system updates status to “delivered”.
8. **Post‑Delivery Email** – request review/rating; offer discount on next purchase.

### 7.3 Automated Notifications
- **Twilio/ Bulksms Ghana** for SMS/USSD alerts (order confirmed, shipped, delivered).
- **Email receipts** via Mailgun or SendGrid.
- **In‑app notifications** for users who have the PWA installed.

### 7.4 Return/Exchange Policy (Clear & Concise)
- **7‑day return window** from delivery date.
- Item must be unworn, unwashed, with original tags.
- Customer bears return shipping cost unless the item is defective or mis‑described.
- Refund processed within 3‑5 business days after receipt inspection.

