## 8. Phase G – Marketing & Growth Strategy (Ghana‑Focused)
### 8.1 Channel Mix
| Channel | Tactics | Expected Impact |
|---------|---------|-----------------|
| **Instagram & TikTok** | • Daily “Dress of the Day” reels showing styling tips.<br>• Customer UGC reposts (how they styled the thrift dress).<br>• Hashtags: `#GhanaFashion #ThriftFinds #OUTFITREPEAT #MadeInGhana`. | High reach among youth; visual showcase essential for fashion. |
| **Facebook Groups & Pages** | • Join “Ghana Fashion Lovers”, “Second‑hand Fashion” groups.<br>• Post new arrivals (adhere to group rules; use paid ads where allowed). | Still the largest marketplace network in Ghana. |
| **Micro‑Influencer Partnerships** | • 5k‑20k fashion/lifestyle influencers. Offer a free dress in exchange for a post/story. | Authentic endorsement; relatively affordable. |
| **WhatsApp Broadcast** | • Broadcast list for “New Arrivals”.<br>• Quick updates on flash sales. | Near‑universal WhatsApp usage; instant delivery. |
| **SEO & Blog** | • Optimize product titles/descriptions with keywords: “affordable thrift dress Ghana”, “used evening gown Accra”.<br>• Blog posts: “How to style a thrift dress for a Ghanaian wedding”. | Capture organic traffic from people searching online. |
| **Offline Pop‑ups** | • Partner with a café or boutique for a one‑day “Thrift Pop‑up”.<br>• Collect emails/phone numbers on‑site. | Builds brand trust; gives tactile experience. |
| **Referral Program** | “Bring a friend – both get GH₵ 10 off next purchase.” | Leverages word‑of‑mouth in tight‑knit communities. |
| **Paid Ads (optional)** | • Facebook/Instagram geo‑targeted ads to Accra, Kumasi, Tamale.<br>• Start with GH₵ 50/day testing creatives. | Quick test of ROI before scaling. |

### 8.2 Launch Checklist
- [ ] **Pre‑launch** – Build “Coming Soon” landing page with email capture (offer “first‑order discount”).
- [ ] **Day 0** – Announce on Instagram, Facebook, Twitter; send press release to local fashion blogs (BellaNaija, ModernGhana).
- [ ] **Week 1‑2** – Run a “7‑day thrift flash sale” (e.g., 20 % off all items) to generate first‑order momentum.
- [ ] **Ongoing** – Post 3‑5 new dresses weekly; engage with comments/DMs; collect reviews for social proof.
- [ ] **Monthly** – Analyze sales data, adjust inventory mix, run a small paid‑ad test, update SEO keywords.

### 8.3 Budget Allocation (Sample First 3 Months)
| Item | Approx. Cost (GH₵) |
|------|-------------------|
| Influencer fees (3 × micro) | 600‑1,200 |
| Facebook/Instagram ads (test) | 500‑1,000 |
| Photography (studio time, props) | 300‑500 |
| SMS notifications (Twilio bulk) | 100‑200 |
| Brand assets (logo, mockups) | 200‑400 |
| **Total** | **≈ GH₵ 1,700‑3,300** |

